%T A401079 27875,40990,59529,85488,121506,171098,238865,330844,454888,621215,
%U A401079 842991,1137199,1525589,2035986,2703794,3574000,4703484,6164080,8046117,10462977,13556502
%N A401079 Number of distinct nonzero tangency polynomials of permutations of length n.
%C A401079 For a permutation pi, the coefficient of x^k in its tangency polynomial counts the number of singular meanders realizing pi with exactly k tangencies. The sequence counts distinct nonzero tangency polynomials.
%H A401079 Yury Belousov, <a href="/A401079/b401079.txt">Table of n, a(n) for n = 1..45</a>
%H A401079 Yury Belousov, <a href="https://github.com/YuryBelousov/s_meandric">C++ code for generating the sequence</a>, GitHub.
%H A401079 Yury Belousov and Viktoriia Georgievskaia, <a href="https://arxiv.org/abs/2609.30068">S-meandric Permutations and Tangency Polynomials</a>, arXiv:2609.30068 [math.CO], 2026.
%F A401079 a(n) = exp(Pi*sqrt(n))/(8*Pi^2)*(log(n)+2*Gamma-2*log(Pi) + O(log(n)/sqrt(n))), where Gamma is Euler's constant.
%e A401079 a(2) = 2. The two distinct tangency polynomials are (1+x)^2 and 2*x.
%Y A401079 Cf. A393122, A400881.
%K A401079 nonn,new
%O A401079 1,2
%A A401079 _Yury Belousov_, Oct 14 2026
